[ ] Run the facilitator as root on the dev pod $Darrion, 2026-10-08: get the dev pod working and the assistant running there as root, working from there. The charter's next practical work: build and boot the dev profile and perform one root-agent task. 2026-10-08: proven once on an ephemeral VM: built, booted, root SSH, Claude Code as root with a tmpfs token, one task harvested and landed (assistant 963ae4a). Remaining for 'run from there': a persistent pod (not --ephemeral) where the facilitator's own session lives, with its memory repo harvested back on a schedule; and where the pod runs (desktop VM vs the dev machine). 2026-10-09: where the pod runs is decided: the NUC, on metal (meta-analysis DECISIONS 03acf7c). Next: bring back the installer and emergency UKI profiles (moved to reference/), rehearse a USB install in a VM, production keys on the desktop, TPM-sealed agent credentials, then install on the NUC. 2026-10-09 (session 9): hardware install rehearsed end to end in QEMU (production keys, raw image on a blank 64G NVMe, ESP null-key SSH credential, TPM root unlock across reboots, recovery key, Secure Boot enrollment from ESP .auth files then enabled (user)). Runbook: docs/install-dev-pod.md. Next: Darrion installs on the NUC with the Arch ISO stick. 2026-10-10: INSTALLED on the NUC (GMKtec NucBox M6) through runbook step 6: image verified by sha256, TPM unlock of root, /home and swap across an unattended reboot, recovery keys for root and /home in 1Password, agent-facilitator with run0. Secure Boot deferred (firmware exposes no SB variables; menu hard to reach). Next: move in (agent-sandbox, TPM-sealed agent credentials, Claude Code, shpool, the assistant repo).$ !2 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-0ffc-7750-887c-9d8d6c3e6dc0
